ion; search prints one service's full telemetry record.\",\n      \"A note: one real production bug that parallel lists could cause, in your own words.\"\n    ],\n    \"acceptance\": [\n      \"Services are stored as a single list of dicts; no parallel lists remain.\",\n      \"All v0.4 features produce identical output on the new shape.\",\n      \"Removing a service by name is one operation and leaves other services intact.\",\n      \"Searching an unknown name prints a clear \\\"service not found\\\" message.\",\n      \"You can explain why structured dict records beat parallel lists, with a concrete failure example.\"\n    ],\n    \"starter\": \"lesson-05-starter.zip\",\n    \"filename\": \"stockbook.py\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"day\": 6,\n    \"title\": \"MetricPulse v0.6 - persistent state & defensive JSON\",\n    \"brief\": \"MetricPulse resets state when it terminates. Build v0.6: on start, load the service catalog from telemetry.json (or start fresh with a clear message if there is no file); after every update, persist; and no malformed input may ever crash it - \\\"three\\\", \\\"-5\\\", and empty input all receive a friendly message.\",\n    \"deliverables\": [\n      \"metricpulse.py loads the service catalog from telemetry.json on start, or starts fresh with a message.\",\n      \"Adding a service saves the file immediately.\",\n      \"A test note: the malformed inputs you tested and what the program printed.\"\n    ],\n    \"acceptance\": [\n      \"Services added in one run are preserved after closing and reopening.\",\n      \"First launch with no save file starts fresh with a clear message.\",\n      \"A corrupt JSON file produces an error message and a fresh start, not an unhandled traceback.\",\n      \"Typing non-numeric strings at a latency prompt shows a message, not a crash.\",\n      \"You can explain what try/except does in one sentence, using the missing file as the example.\"\n    ],\n    \"starter\": \"lesson-06-starter.zip\",\n    \"filename\