he current FastAPI installation command in the linked documentation.\",\n    \"deliverables\": [\n      \"An API contract and runnable FastAPI service with documented setup.\",\n      \"A durable feedback schema and parameterized storage layer.\",\n      \"Request validation and explicitly scoped access checks.\",\n      \"HTTP, restart, and invalid-input test results.\"\n    ],\n    \"acceptance\": [\n      \"The three endpoints follow documented request/response contracts.\",\n      \"Invalid payloads and domain-rule failures are rejected clearly.\",\n      \"Feedback survives a process restart in the documented database.\",\n      \"Database values use parameterized SQL rather than command concatenation.\",\n      \"Trusted identity or fixture limits and access checks are explicitly tested.\"\n    ],\n    \"starter\": \"lesson-24-starter.zip\",\n    \"filename\": \"feedback_store.py\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"day\": 25,\n    \"title\": \"Request tracing and an incident runbook\",\n    \"brief\": \"Instrument the fictional assistant's validation, retrieval, answer, and failure stages with structured events and a shared request ID. Create a runbook for a retrieval timeout and a bad release. Measure actual elapsed time where implemented, clearly label fixtures, and avoid unnecessary private content in logs.\",\n    \"deliverables\": [\n      \"A structured event schema and correlated request trace.\",\n      \"A redaction/data-minimization policy for logs.\",\n      \"Runbooks for timeout diagnosis and release recovery.\",\n      \"Evidence from a simulated incident and runbook walkthrough.\"\n    ],\n    \"acceptance\": [\n      \"Events from one request share a correlation ID.\",\n      \"Stable event names identify success and failure stages.\",\n      \"Logs omit credentials and unnecessary private content.\",\n      \"Actual measurements and fixture values are clearly distinguished.\",\n      \"Runbooks include symptoms, checks, recovery verification, and ownership.\"